#
# muir-ah as the associated machine of a System 304 band (DESIGN.md §8).
# A file of flags, as system-100.muir-ahrc is, which says more of what
# each line is for.
#
# The numbers are the band's own, asked at its listener, since its host
# table is in the pack and not in the sources: the band is AMS-LISPM-1 at
# 4401, and looks for its files and its time at 4403, OZ --- AMS-BRIDGE-1
# under its other name (muir's src/chaos/mod.rs). This host is that one.

--address 4403

# OZ first, the name muir's own server answers STATUS with for this band.
# Unverified: whether OZ is that host's own name in the band's table or a
# nickname of AMS-BRIDGE-1 (muir's tests/cc_harness), which
# (si:get-host-from-address #o4403 :chaos) at the band's listener would
# settle.
#
# No system=: what the band's table gives this host is not known. That
# table is in the pack; the one in this release's sources,
# sys/site/hosts.text, is MIT's, which has MIT-OZ as TOPS-20 at 11406 and
# nothing at 4403. The same host sent :system-type at the listener would
# give it. Without one, HOSTAB answers this host's names with no
# SYSTEM-TYPE.
--name    OZ,AMS-BRIDGE-1

# Without a --listen line, 127.0.0.1:42042 (DESIGN.md §5):
#--listen 192.0.2.10

# The homes in the base, writable; the release's sources mounted at /sys,
# read-only, because the band asks for them as /sys/... (muir's
# --chaos-file-root help), and where muir's own vendor/run/file-root links
# sys.
--root    /srv/lispm
--root    sys=/path/to/muir/vendor/system-304-0/sys-304-0,ro

# The band's machine. Its system type is not read from the band: LISPM is
# what System 100's table gives its Lisp Machine, taken as this one's.
--host    4401,AMS-LISPM-1,system=LISPM

# A muir run for this band, on this host (DESIGN.md §9):
#
#   muir --disk-pack /path/to/muir/vendor/run/disk-sys-304-0.img \
#        --chaos-address 4401 --chaos-udp 42043 \
#        --chaos-udp-peer 4403@127.0.0.1:42042
#
# --chaos-address 4401 without its ,<server> half leaves muir's own server
# at 177002, out of the band's way, so the band's calls to 4403 come here.
